  ('a0000003-0000-4000-8000-0000000003e0', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000003', 'vocabulary', 'N3', '{"word":"試す","reading":"ためす","meaning":"To try (out), have a try (at), or test.","partOfSpeech":"う verb","frequencyRank":1854,"mnemonic":"Imagine 試す as a button labeled ''tamesu''; press it and the room instantly demonstrates try (out), have a try (at), or test with too much confidence.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":2,"pitchAccent":"nakadaka","nuance":"Use 試す for the action or change of try (out), have a try (at), or test. The dictionary form is useful before grammar like こと, while polite sentences usually change the ending. Focus on the core action shown in the example.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"試してみる。","en":"I try.","furigana":"ためしてみる。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"試","radical":"言","meaning":"test","reading":"ため"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000003-0000-4000-8000-0000000003e1', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000003', 'vocabulary', 'N3', '{"word":"便り","reading":"たより","meaning":"News, tidings, or information.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Think of 便り shouting ''tayori'' from a billboard whenever news, tidings, or information appears, as if vocabulary needed dramatic advertising.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":1,"pitchAccent":"atamadaka","nuance":"Use 便り as the basic noun for news, tidings, or information. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"便りをください。","en":"Keep in touch.","furigana":"たよりをください。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"便","radical":"人","meaning":"convenience","reading":"たよ"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000003-0000-4000-8000-0000000003e2', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000003', 'vocabulary', 'N3', '{"word":"頼る","reading":"たよる","meaning":"To rely on, depend on, or count on.","partOfSpeech":"う verb","frequencyRank":2633,"mnemonic":"See 頼る on a sticky note stuck to rely on, depend on, or count on; the note keeps saying ''tayoru'' until the sound refuses to leave.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":2,"pitchAccent":"nakadaka","nuance":"Use 頼る for the action or change of rely on, depend on, or count on. The dictionary form is useful before grammar like こと, while polite sentences usually change the ending. Focus on the core action shown in the example.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"もっと頼って欲しかった。","en":"I needed you to rely on me more.","furigana":"もっとたよってほしかった。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"頼","radical":"頁","meaning":"trust","reading":"たよ"}]}'::jsonb),
