  ('a0000003-0000-4000-8000-000000000681', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000003', 'vocabulary', 'N3', '{"word":"別れ","reading":"わかれ","meaning":"Parting, separation, or farewell.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":3071,"mnemonic":"Picture a tiny teacher pointing at 別れ and saying ''wakare'' while acting out parting, separation, or farewell with ridiculous seriousness.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":3,"pitchAccent":"nakadaka","nuance":"Use 別れ as the basic noun for parting, separation, or farewell. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"彼に別れを告げた。","en":"I took leave of him.","furigana":"かれにわかれをつげた。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"別","radical":"刀","meaning":"separate","reading":"わか"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000003-0000-4000-8000-000000000682', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000003', 'vocabulary', 'N3', '{"word":"我儘","reading":"わがまま","meaning":"Selfish or egoist.","partOfSpeech":"な adjective","frequencyRank":3475,"mnemonic":"Picture 我儘 wearing a name tag that says ''wagamama'', proudly announcing selfish or egoist like it just won a tiny game show.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":4,"pitchAccent":"nakadaka","nuance":"Use 我儘 to describe something as selfish or egoist. It attaches to simple descriptions and noun phrases, so it is most useful when you want to state a visible quality, condition, feeling, or character.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"わがままね。","en":"You''re selfish.","furigana":"わがままね。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"我","radical":"戈","meaning":"ego","reading":"われ"},{"kanji":"儘","radical":"人","meaning":"as it is","reading":"まま"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000003-0000-4000-8000-000000000683', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000003', 'vocabulary', 'N3', '{"word":"脇","reading":"わき","meaning":"Armpit, under one''s arm, or side.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":2722,"mnemonic":"Imagine 脇 as a button labeled ''waki''; press it and the room instantly demonstrates armpit, under one''s arm, or side with too much confidence.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use 脇 as the basic noun for armpit, under one''s arm, or side. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"脇によってください。","en":"Please step aside.","furigana":"わきによってください。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"脇","radical":"肉","meaning":"armpit","reading":"わき"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000003-0000-4000-8000-000000000684', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000003', 'vocabulary', 'N3', '{"word":"分ける","reading":"わける","meaning":"To divide (into), split (into), or part.","partOfSpeech":"る verb","frequencyRank":1038,"mnemonic":"Think of 分ける shouting ''wakeru'' from a billboard whenever divide (into), split (into), or part appears, as if vocabulary needed dramatic advertising.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":2,"pitchAccent":"nakadaka","nuance":"Use 分ける for the action or change of divide (into), split (into), or part. The dictionary form is useful before grammar like こと, while polite sentences usually change the ending. Focus on the core action shown in the example.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"よく分けることがあります。","en":"There are times when someone may divide (into), split (into), or part.","furigana":"よくわけることがあります。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"分","radical":"刀","meaning":"part","reading":"わ"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000003-0000-4000-8000-000000000685', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000003', 'vocabulary', 'N3', '{"word":"態と","reading":"わざと","meaning":"On purpose, deliberately, or intentionally.","partOfSpeech":"Adverb","frequencyRank":3840,"mnemonic":"See 態と on a sticky note stuck to on purpose, deliberately, or intentionally; the note keeps saying ''wazato'' until the sound refuses to leave.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":1,"pitchAccent":"atamadaka","nuance":"Use 態と to adjust how an action, state, or whole sentence feels. It usually sits near the verb or adjective it modifies and adds timing, degree, manner, or speaker attitude.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"わざと間違えたの？","en":"Did you purposefully make a mistake?","furigana":"わざとまちがえたの？"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"態","radical":"心","meaning":"attitude","reading":"わざ"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000003-0000-4000-8000-000000000686', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000003', 'vocabulary', 'N3', '{"word":"僅か","reading":"わずか","meaning":"A little, a few, or small.","partOfSpeech":"な adjective","frequencyRank":1144,"mnemonic":"Picture a tiny teacher pointing at 僅か and saying ''wazuka'' while acting out a little, a few, or small with ridiculous seriousness.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":1,"pitchAccent":"atamadaka","nuance":"Use 僅か to describe something as a little, a few, or small. It attaches to simple descriptions and noun phrases, so it is most useful when you want to state a visible quality, condition, feeling, or character.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"わずかな収入で暮らしていくのは苦しい。","en":"It''s hard for me to live on my small income.","furigana":"わずかなしゅうにゅうでくらしていくのはくるしい。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"僅","radical":"人","meaning":"a wee bit","reading":"わず"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000003-0000-4000-8000-000000000687', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000003', 'vocabulary', 'N3', '{"word":"綿","reading":"わた","meaning":"Cotton plant (Gossypium spp.).","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Picture 綿 wearing a name tag that says ''wata'', proudly announcing cotton plant (Gossypium spp.) like it just won a tiny game show.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":2,"pitchAccent":"nakadaka","nuance":"Use 綿 as the basic noun for cotton plant (Gossypium spp.). It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"綿は水を吸い込む。","en":"Cotton sucks up water.","furigana":"めんはみずをすいこむ。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"綿","radical":"糸","meaning":"cotton","reading":"わた"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000003-0000-4000-8000-000000000688', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000003', 'vocabulary', 'N3', '{"word":"話題","reading":"わだい","meaning":"Topic or subject.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":1089,"mnemonic":"Imagine 話題 as a button labeled ''wadai''; press it and the room instantly demonstrates topic or subject with too much confidence.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use 話題 as the basic noun for topic or subject. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"話題変えよう。","en":"Let''s change the topic.","furigana":"わだいかえよう。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"話","radical":"言","meaning":"tale","reading":"はなす"},{"kanji":"題","radical":"頁","meaning":"topic","reading":"ダイ"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000003-0000-4000-8000-000000000689', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000003', 'vocabulary', 'N3', '{"word":"笑い","reading":"わらい","meaning":"Laugh or laughter.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":563,"mnemonic":"Think of 笑い shouting ''warai'' from a billboard whenever laugh or laughter appears, as if vocabulary needed dramatic advertising.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use 笑い as the basic noun for laugh or laughter. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"笑いは移る。","en":"Laughter is infectious.","furigana":"わらいはうつる。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"笑","radical":"竹","meaning":"laugh","reading":"わら"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000003-0000-4000-8000-00000000068a', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000003', 'vocabulary', 'N3', '{"word":"割る","reading":"わる","meaning":"To divide.","partOfSpeech":"う verb","frequencyRank":2661,"mnemonic":"See 割る on a sticky note stuck to divide; the note keeps saying ''waru'' until the sound refuses to leave.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use 割る for the action or change of divide. The dictionary form is useful before grammar like こと, while polite sentences usually change the ending. Focus on the core action shown in the example.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"灰皿を割ってしまいました。","en":"I broke your ashtray.","furigana":"はいざらをわってしまいました。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"割","radical":"刀","meaning":"proportion","reading":"わ"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000003-0000-4000-8000-00000000068b', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000003', 'vocabulary', 'N3', '{"word":"悪口","reading":"わるぐち","meaning":"(verbal) abuse, speaking ill of people, or bad-mouthing.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Picture a tiny teacher pointing at 悪口 and saying ''waruguchi'' while acting out (verbal) abuse, speaking ill of people, or bad-mouthing with ridiculous seriousness.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":2,"pitchAccent":"nakadaka","nuance":"Use 悪口 as the basic noun for (verbal) abuse, speaking ill of people, or bad-mouthing. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"トムの悪口はやめて！","en":"Stop bad mouthing Tom.","furigana":"トムのわるぐちはやめて！"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"悪","radical":"心","meaning":"bad","reading":"わるい"},{"kanji":"口","radical":"口","meaning":"mouth","reading":"くち"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000003-0000-4000-8000-00000000068c', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000003', 'vocabulary', 'N3', '{"word":"我々","reading":"われわれ","meaning":"We.","partOfSpeech":"Expression","frequencyRank":527,"mnemonic":"Picture 我々 wearing a name tag that says ''wareware'', proudly announcing we like it just won a tiny game show.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use 我々 as a set expression in common conversation. It carries its meaning as a whole phrase, so it is best learned with short examples and the situation where it naturally appears.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"我々は技術を後世に伝えなければならない。","en":"We must hand down our craft to posterity.","furigana":"われわれはぎじゅつをこうせいにつたえなければならない。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"我","radical":"戈","meaning":"ego","reading":"われ"},{"kanji":"々","radical":null,"meaning":null,"reading":null}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000003-0000-4000-8000-00000000068d', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000003', 'vocabulary', 'N3', '{"word":"湾","reading":"わん","meaning":"Bay, gulf, or inlet.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Imagine 湾 as a button labeled ''wan''; press it and the room instantly demonstrates bay, gulf, or inlet with too much confidence.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":1,"pitchAccent":"atamadaka","nuance":"Use 湾 as the basic noun for bay, gulf, or inlet. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"その空港は大阪湾にあります。","en":"The airport is in Osaka Bay.","furigana":"そのくうこうはおおさかわんにあります。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"湾","radical":"水","meaning":"gulf","reading":"わん"}]}'::jsonb)
