  ('a0000002-0000-4000-8000-0000000003f9', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000002', 'vocabulary', 'N2', '{"word":"吊るす","reading":"つるす","meaning":"To hang or hang up.","partOfSpeech":"う verb","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Imagine 吊るす as a button labeled ''tsurusu''; press it and the room instantly demonstrates hang or hang up with too much confidence.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use 吊るす for the action or change of hang or hang up. The dictionary form is useful before grammar like こと, while polite sentences usually change the ending. Focus on the core action shown in the example.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"私はシャツを吊るしている。","en":"I''m hanging up my shirts.","furigana":"わたしはシャツをつるしている。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"吊","radical":"口","meaning":"suspend","reading":"つ"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000002-0000-4000-8000-0000000003fa', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000002', 'vocabulary', 'N2', '{"word":"手洗い","reading":"てあらい","meaning":"Washing one''s hands or water (or basin, etc.) for washing one''s hands.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Think of 手洗い shouting ''tearai'' from a billboard whenever washing one''s hands or water (or basin, etc.) for washing one''s hands appears, as if vocabulary needed dramatic advertising.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":2,"pitchAccent":"nakadaka","nuance":"Use 手洗い as the basic noun for washing one''s hands or water (or basin, etc.) for washing one''s hands. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"お手洗いは、左側です。","en":"The restrooms are on the left.","furigana":"おてあらいは、ひだりがわです。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"手","radical":"手","meaning":"hand","reading":"て"},{"kanji":"洗","radical":"水","meaning":"wash","reading":"あらう"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000002-0000-4000-8000-0000000003fb', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000002', 'vocabulary', 'N2', '{"word":"定員","reading":"ていいん","meaning":"Fixed number (of people), prescribed number, or quota.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":2370,"mnemonic":"See 定員 on a sticky note stuck to fixed number (of people), prescribed number, or quota; the note keeps saying ''teiin'' until the sound refuses to leave.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use 定員 as the basic noun for fixed number (of people), prescribed number, or quota. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"ボートは定員オーバーでバランスを失った。","en":"The boat was off balance because it was overloaded.","furigana":"ボートはていいんオーバーでバランスをうしなった。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"定","radical":"宀","meaning":"determine","reading":"さだめる"},{"kanji":"員","radical":"口","meaning":"employee","reading":"イン"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000002-0000-4000-8000-0000000003fc', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000002', 'vocabulary', 'N2', '{"word":"低下","reading":"ていか","meaning":"Fall, decline, or lowering.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":1555,"mnemonic":"Picture a tiny teacher pointing at 低下 and saying ''teika'' while acting out fall, decline, or lowering with ridiculous seriousness.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use 低下 as the basic noun for fall, decline, or lowering. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"視力が低下してきたんです。","en":"My eyesight is getting worse.","furigana":"しりょくがていかしてきたんです。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"低","radical":"人","meaning":"lower","reading":"ひくい"},{"kanji":"下","radical":"一","meaning":"below","reading":"した"}]}'::jsonb),
