  ('a0000002-0000-4000-8000-00000000065c', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000002', 'vocabulary', 'N2', '{"word":"詫びる","reading":"わびる","meaning":"To apologize, apologise, or make an apology.","partOfSpeech":"る verb","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Think of 詫びる shouting ''wabiru'' from a billboard whenever apologize, apologise, or make an apology appears, as if vocabulary needed dramatic advertising.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use 詫びる for the action or change of apologize, apologise, or make an apology. The dictionary form is useful before grammar like こと, while polite sentences usually change the ending. Focus on the core action shown in the example.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"彼は無礼を詫びた。","en":"He apologized for his rudeness.","furigana":"かれはぶれいをわびた。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"詫","radical":"言","meaning":"apologize","reading":"わ"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000002-0000-4000-8000-00000000065d', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000002', 'vocabulary', 'N2', '{"word":"和服","reading":"わふく","meaning":"Japanese clothes.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"See 和服 on a sticky note stuck to japanese clothes; the note keeps saying ''wafuku'' until the sound refuses to leave.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use 和服 as the basic noun for japanese clothes. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"洋服は和服より働きやすい。","en":"Western clothes are easier to work in than Japanese clothes.","furigana":"ようふくはわふくよりはたらきやすい。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"和","radical":"口","meaning":"harmony","reading":"やわらぐ"},{"kanji":"服","radical":"月","meaning":"clothing","reading":"フク"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000002-0000-4000-8000-00000000065e', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000002', 'vocabulary', 'N2', '{"word":"割合に","reading":"わりあいに","meaning":"Comparatively.","partOfSpeech":"Adverb","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Picture a tiny teacher pointing at 割合に and saying ''wariaini'' while acting out comparatively with ridiculous seriousness.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":null,"pitchAccent":null,"nuance":"Use 割合に to adjust how an action, state, or whole sentence feels. It usually sits near the verb or adjective it modifies and adds timing, degree, manner, or speaker attitude.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"割合に使います。","en":"I use it comparatively.","furigana":"わりあいにつかいます。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"割","radical":"刀","meaning":"proportion","reading":"わる"},{"kanji":"合","radical":"口","meaning":"fit","reading":"あう"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000002-0000-4000-8000-00000000065f', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000002', 'vocabulary', 'N2', '{"word":"割り算","reading":"わりざん","meaning":"Division.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Picture 割り算 wearing a name tag that says ''warizan'', proudly announcing division like it just won a tiny game show.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":2,"pitchAccent":"nakadaka","nuance":"Use 割り算 as the basic noun for division. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"何らかの数字をゼロで割り算すると未定義の解になる。","en":"If you divide any number by zero, the result is undefined.","furigana":"なんらかのすうじをゼロでわりざんするとみていぎのかいになる。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"割","radical":"刀","meaning":"proportion","reading":"わ"},{"kanji":"算","radical":"竹","meaning":"calculate","reading":"ざん"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000660', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000002', 'vocabulary', 'N2', '{"word":"割と","reading":"わりと","meaning":"Comparatively, relatively, or fairly.","partOfSpeech":"Adverb","frequencyRank":625,"mnemonic":"Imagine 割と as a button labeled ''warito''; press it and the room instantly demonstrates comparatively, relatively, or fairly with too much confidence.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use 割と to adjust how an action, state, or whole sentence feels. It usually sits near the verb or adjective it modifies and adds timing, degree, manner, or speaker attitude.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"トムって割と早口だね。","en":"Tom speaks relatively fast.","furigana":"トムってわりとはやくちだね。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"割","radical":"刀","meaning":"proportion","reading":"わり"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000661', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000002', 'vocabulary', 'N2', '{"word":"割引","reading":"わりびき","meaning":"Discount, reduction, or rebate.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Think of 割引 shouting ''waribiki'' from a billboard whenever discount, reduction, or rebate appears, as if vocabulary needed dramatic advertising.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use 割引 as the basic noun for discount, reduction, or rebate. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"学生割引はありますか。","en":"Do you have a student fare?","furigana":"がくせいわりびきはありますか。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"割","radical":"刀","meaning":"proportion","reading":"わる"},{"kanji":"引","radical":"弓","meaning":"pull","reading":"ひく"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000662', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000002', 'vocabulary', 'N2', '{"word":"椀","reading":"わん","meaning":"Bowl (wooden).","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"See 椀 on a sticky note stuck to bowl (wooden); the note keeps saying ''wan'' until the sound refuses to leave.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use 椀 as the basic noun for bowl (wooden). It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"おっぱいがお椀型で羨ましいなあ。","en":"I''m so jealous of your bowl-shaped boobs.","furigana":"おっぱいがおわんがたでうらやましいなあ。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"椀","radical":"木","meaning":"wooden or lacquered bowl","reading":"わん"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000002-0000-4000-8000-000000000663', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000002', 'vocabulary', 'N2', '{"word":"碗","reading":"わん","meaning":"Bowl (ceramic, porcelain).","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Picture a tiny teacher pointing at 碗 and saying ''wan'' while acting out bowl (ceramic, porcelain) with ridiculous seriousness.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use 碗 as the basic noun for bowl (ceramic, porcelain). It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"わんこ欲しい。","en":"I want a doggy.","furigana":"わんこほしい。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"碗","radical":"石","meaning":"porcelain bowl","reading":"わん"}]}'::jsonb)
