  ('a0000001-0000-4000-8000-0000000003e9', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000001', 'vocabulary', 'N1', '{"word":"然も","reading":"さも","meaning":"Really (seem, appear, etc.), truly, or evidently.","partOfSpeech":"Adverb","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Picture 然も wearing a name tag that says ''samo'', proudly announcing really (seem, appear, etc.), truly, or evidently like it just won a tiny game show.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":1,"pitchAccent":"atamadaka","nuance":"Use 然も to adjust how an action, state, or whole sentence feels. It usually sits near the verb or adjective it modifies and adds timing, degree, manner, or speaker attitude.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"黙っていなさい。さもないと叱られるよ。","en":"Hold your tongue, or you''ll be punished.","furigana":"だまっていなさい。さもないとしかられるよ。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"然","radical":"火","meaning":"sort of thing","reading":"さ"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000001-0000-4000-8000-0000000003ea', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000001', 'vocabulary', 'N1', '{"word":"作用","reading":"さよう","meaning":"Action, operation, or process.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":2932,"mnemonic":"Imagine 作用 as a button labeled ''sayou''; press it and the room instantly demonstrates action, operation, or process with too much confidence.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":1,"pitchAccent":"atamadaka","nuance":"Use 作用 as the basic noun for action, operation, or process. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"日光は皮膚に作用する。","en":"The sunbeam acts upon the skin.","furigana":"にっこうはひふにさようする。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"作","radical":"人","meaning":"make","reading":"つくる"},{"kanji":"用","radical":"用","meaning":"utilize","reading":"もちいる"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000001-0000-4000-8000-0000000003eb', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000001', 'vocabulary', 'N1', '{"word":"障る","reading":"さわる","meaning":"To be harmful to, hinder, or interfere with.","partOfSpeech":"う verb","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Think of 障る shouting ''sawaru'' from a billboard whenever be harmful to, hinder, or interfere with appears, as if vocabulary needed dramatic advertising.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use 障る for the action or change of be harmful to, hinder, or interfere with. The dictionary form is useful before grammar like こと, while polite sentences usually change the ending. Focus on the core action shown in the example.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"気に障ったならごめん。","en":"I''m sorry if I hurt your feelings.","furigana":"きにさわったならごめん。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"障","radical":"阜","meaning":"hinder","reading":"さわ"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000001-0000-4000-8000-0000000003ec', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000001', 'vocabulary', 'N1', '{"word":"さん","reading":"さん","meaning":"Mr, Mrs, or Miss.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"See さん on a sticky note stuck to mr, Mrs, or Miss; the note keeps saying ''san'' until the sound refuses to leave.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use さん as the basic noun for mr, Mrs, or Miss. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"参議院はどんな改正案も通さなくても構わないようです。","en":"The Upper House seems bent on defeating any reform bills.","furigana":"さんぎいんはどんなかいせいあんもとおさなくてもかまわないようです。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000001-0000-4000-8000-0000000003ed', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000001', 'vocabulary', 'N1', '{"word":"サン","reading":"サン","meaning":"Sun.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Picture a tiny teacher pointing at サン and saying ''san'' while acting out sun with ridiculous seriousness.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":null,"pitchAccent":null,"nuance":"Use サン as the basic noun for sun. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"ミャンマーの民主化運動指導者アウン・サン・スー・チーは10年以上監禁されている。","en":"The leader of Myanmar''s pro-democracy movement, Aung San Suu Kyi, has been in detainment for over 10 years.","furigana":"ミャンマーのみんしゅかうんどうしどうしゃアウン・サン・スー・チーは10ねんいじょうかんきんされている。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000001-0000-4000-8000-0000000003ee', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000001', 'vocabulary', 'N1', '{"word":"酸","reading":"さん","meaning":"Acid.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Picture 酸 wearing a name tag that says ''san'', proudly announcing acid like it just won a tiny game show.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":1,"pitchAccent":"atamadaka","nuance":"Use 酸 as the basic noun for acid. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"酸は金属を侵す。","en":"Acids act on metals.","furigana":"さんはきんぞくをおかす。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"酸","radical":"酉","meaning":"acid","reading":"さん"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000001-0000-4000-8000-0000000003ef', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000001', 'vocabulary', 'N1', '{"word":"酸化","reading":"さんか","meaning":"Oxidation or oxidization.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Imagine 酸化 as a button labeled ''sanka''; press it and the room instantly demonstrates oxidation or oxidization with too much confidence.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use 酸化 as the basic noun for oxidation or oxidization. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"アルコールが酸化するとアルデヒドとなりますが、アルデヒドが酸化するとどうなりますか。","en":"If you oxidise an alcohol you get an aldehyde but what do you get if you oxidise an aldehyde?","furigana":"アルコールがさんかするとアルデヒドとなりますが、アルデヒドがさんかするとどうなりますか。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"酸","radical":"酉","meaning":"acid","reading":"すい"},{"kanji":"化","radical":"匕","meaning":"change","reading":"ばける"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000001-0000-4000-8000-0000000003f0', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000001', 'vocabulary', 'N1', '{"word":"山岳","reading":"さんがく","meaning":"Mountain chain or mountains.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Think of 山岳 shouting ''sangaku'' from a billboard whenever mountain chain or mountains appears, as if vocabulary needed dramatic advertising.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use 山岳 as the basic noun for mountain chain or mountains. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"山岳救助隊は２４時間待機している。","en":"The mountain rescue team is on call 24 hours a day.","furigana":"さんがくきゅうじょたいはにじゅうよじかんたいきしている。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"山","radical":"山","meaning":"mountain","reading":"やま"},{"kanji":"岳","radical":"山","meaning":"point","reading":"たけ"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000001-0000-4000-8000-0000000003f1', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000001', 'vocabulary', 'N1', '{"word":"産休","reading":"さんきゅう","meaning":"Maternity leave or paternity leave.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"See 産休 on a sticky note stuck to maternity leave or paternity leave; the note keeps saying ''sankyuu'' until the sound refuses to leave.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use 産休 as the basic noun for maternity leave or paternity leave. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"彼女は来週から産休に入る。","en":"She will start her maternity leave next week.","furigana":"かのじょはらいしゅうからさんきゅうにはいる。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"産","radical":"生","meaning":"products","reading":"うむ"},{"kanji":"休","radical":"人","meaning":"rest","reading":"やすむ"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000001-0000-4000-8000-0000000003f2', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000001', 'vocabulary', 'N1', '{"word":"サンキュー","reading":"サンキュー","meaning":"Thank you or thanks.","partOfSpeech":"Expression","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Picture a tiny teacher pointing at サンキュー and saying ''sankyu-'' while acting out thank you or thanks with ridiculous seriousness.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":null,"pitchAccent":null,"nuance":"Use サンキュー as a set expression in common conversation. It carries its meaning as a whole phrase, so it is best learned with short examples and the situation where it naturally appears.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"サンキュー。","en":"Thank you or thanks.","furigana":"サンキュー。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000001-0000-4000-8000-0000000003f3', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000001', 'vocabulary', 'N1', '{"word":"参議院","reading":"さんぎいん","meaning":"House of Councillors.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Picture 参議院 wearing a name tag that says ''sangiin'', proudly announcing house of Councillors like it just won a tiny game show.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":null,"pitchAccent":null,"nuance":"Use 参議院 as the basic noun for house of Councillors. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"今週は参議院選挙が開かれる。","en":"The house of councillors election opens this week.","furigana":"こんしゅうはさんぎいんせんきょがひらかれる。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"参","radical":"厶","meaning":"nonplussed","reading":"まいる"},{"kanji":"議","radical":"言","meaning":"deliberation","reading":"ギ"},{"kanji":"院","radical":"阜","meaning":"Inst.","reading":"イン"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000001-0000-4000-8000-0000000003f4', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000001', 'vocabulary', 'N1', '{"word":"産後","reading":"さんご","meaning":"After childbirth or postpartum.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Imagine 産後 as a button labeled ''sango''; press it and the room instantly demonstrates after childbirth or postpartum with too much confidence.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":0,"pitchAccent":"heiban","nuance":"Use 産後 as the basic noun for after childbirth or postpartum. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"女性は産後すぐに亡くなった。","en":"The woman died shortly after giving birth.","furigana":"じょせいはさんごすぐになくなった。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"産","radical":"生","meaning":"products","reading":"うむ"},{"kanji":"後","radical":"彳","meaning":"behind","reading":"のち"}]}'::jsonb),
