  ('a0000001-0000-4000-8000-0000000007d1', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000001', 'vocabulary', 'N1', '{"word":"馴れ馴れしい","reading":"なれなれしい","meaning":"Overly familiar, overfamiliar, or too friendly.","partOfSpeech":"い adjective","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Picture 馴れ馴れしい wearing a name tag that says ''narenareshii'', proudly announcing overly familiar, overfamiliar, or too friendly like it just won a tiny game show.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":5,"pitchAccent":"nakadaka","nuance":"Use 馴れ馴れしい to describe something as overly familiar, overfamiliar, or too friendly. It attaches to simple descriptions and noun phrases, so it is most useful when you want to state a visible quality, condition, feeling, or character.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"馴れ馴れしくしないで。","en":"Don''t be fresh with me.","furigana":"なれなれしくしないで。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"馴","radical":"馬","meaning":"get used to","reading":"な"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000001-0000-4000-8000-0000000007d2', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000001', 'vocabulary', 'N1', '{"word":"難","reading":"なん","meaning":"Difficulty, trouble, or hardship.","partOfSpeech":"Noun","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Imagine 難 as a button labeled ''nan''; press it and the room instantly demonstrates difficulty, trouble, or hardship with too much confidence.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":1,"pitchAccent":"atamadaka","nuance":"Use 難 as the basic noun for difficulty, trouble, or hardship. It names a person, thing, place, time, or idea directly, and it commonly appears with particles or です in simple sentences.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"近頃は就職難だ。","en":"Nowadays jobs are hard to come by.","furigana":"ちかごろはしゅうしょくなんだ。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"難","radical":"隹","meaning":"difficult","reading":"なん"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000001-0000-4000-8000-0000000007d3', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000001', 'vocabulary', 'N1', '{"word":"なんか","reading":"なんか","meaning":"Something like, things like, or someone like.","partOfSpeech":"Particle","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Think of なんか shouting ''nanka'' from a billboard whenever something like, things like, or someone like appears, as if vocabulary needed dramatic advertising.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":1,"pitchAccent":"atamadaka","nuance":"Use なんか as a function word that connects sentence parts. Its meaning depends on the role it marks, so pay attention to the words around it and the simple sentence pattern in the example.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"なんか言った？","en":"Did you say something?","furigana":"なんかいった？"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000001-0000-4000-8000-0000000007d4', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000001', 'vocabulary', 'N1', '{"word":"ナンセンス","reading":"ナンセンス","meaning":"Nonsense.","partOfSpeech":"な adjective","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"See ナンセンス on a sticky note stuck to nonsense; the note keeps saying ''nansensu'' until the sound refuses to leave.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":null,"pitchAccent":null,"nuance":"Use ナンセンス to describe something as nonsense. It attaches to simple descriptions and noun phrases, so it is most useful when you want to state a visible quality, condition, feeling, or character.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"それはナンセンスだ。ばか者以外の誰もそれを信じないであろう。","en":"That''s nonsense. Nobody but a fool would believe it.","furigana":"それはナンセンスだ。ばかしゃいがいのだれもそれをしんじないであろう。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000001-0000-4000-8000-0000000007d5', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000001', 'vocabulary', 'N1', '{"word":"何だか","reading":"なんだか","meaning":"(a) little, somewhat, or somehow.","partOfSpeech":"Adverb","frequencyRank":1917,"mnemonic":"Picture a tiny teacher pointing at 何だか and saying ''nandaka'' while acting out (a) little, somewhat, or somehow with ridiculous seriousness.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":null,"pitchAccent":null,"nuance":"Use 何だか to adjust how an action, state, or whole sentence feels. It usually sits near the verb or adjective it modifies and adds timing, degree, manner, or speaker attitude.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"何だか疲れました。","en":"I''m sort of tired.","furigana":"なんだかつかれました。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"何","radical":"人","meaning":"what","reading":"なん"}]}'::jsonb),
  ('a0000001-0000-4000-8000-0000000007d6', '11111111-1111-4111-8111-000000000001', 'vocabulary', 'N1', '{"word":"何だかんだ","reading":"なんだかんだ","meaning":"Something or other, one thing or another, or this or that.","partOfSpeech":"Adverb","frequencyRank":null,"mnemonic":"Picture 何だかんだ wearing a name tag that says ''nandakanda'', proudly announcing something or other, one thing or another, or this or that like it just won a tiny game show.","picture":null,"pitchPosition":null,"pitchAccent":null,"nuance":"Use 何だかんだ to adjust how an action, state, or whole sentence feels. It usually sits near the verb or adjective it modifies and adds timing, degree, manner, or speaker attitude.","exampleSentences":[{"ja":"彼は、なんだかんだ言って支払いを延期した。","en":"He delayed payment on some pretext or other.","furigana":"かれは、なんだかんだいってしはらいをえんきした。"}],"kanjiBreakdown":[{"kanji":"何","radical":"人","meaning":"what","reading":"なん"}]}'::jsonb),
